  "text": "Assistant: Let's reason step by step.\n\n1. **Simplify the numerator:**\n   \\(\\sqrt[3]{4} + \\sqrt[3]{8}\\)\n   Since \\(8 = 2^3\\) and \\(4 = 2^2\\), we have:\n   \\(\\sqrt[3]{4} = \\sqrt[3]{2^2} = 2^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\)\n   \\(\\sqrt[3]{8} = \\sqrt[3]{2^3} = 2^1 = 2\\)\n   So, the numerator simplifies to:\n   \\(2^{\\frac{2}{3}} + 2\\)\n\n2. **Simplify the denominator:**\n   \\(\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}\\)\n   Since \\(9 = 3^2\\) and \\(6\\) remains as is, we have:\n   \\(\\sqrt[3]{9} = 3^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\)\n   \\(\\sqrt[3]{6}\\) remains as is.\n   So, the denominator simplifies to:\n   \\(3^{\\frac{2}{3}} - \\sqrt[3]{6}\\)\n\n3. **Simplify the entire fraction:**\n   We have \\(\\frac{2^{\\frac{2}{3}} + 2}{3^{\\frac{2}{3}} - \\sqrt[3]{6}}\\). To make this a single cube root fraction, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\((3^{\\frac{2}{3}} + \\sqrt[3]{6})\\):\n\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(3^{\\frac{2}{3}} + 2)(3^{\\frac{2}{3}} + \\sqrt[3]{6})}{(3^{\\frac{2}{3}} - \\sqrt[3]{6})(3^{\\frac{2}{3}} + \\sqrt[3]{6})}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the denominator:**\n   The denominator simplifies the cube root expression:\n   \\[\n   (3^{\\frac{2}{3}})^2 - (\\sqrt[3]{6})^2 = 3^{\\frac{4}{3}} - 6^{\\frac{2}{3}}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the numerator:**\n   The numerator simplifies as a Binomial square:\n   \\[\n   (3^{\\frac{2}{3}} + \\sqrt[3]{6}) \\left(3^{\\frac{2}{3}} + \\sqrt[3]{6}\\right) = 3^{\\frac{4}{3}} + 2 \\cdot 3^{\\frac{2}{3}} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + 6^{\\frac{2}{3}}\n   \\]\n   Given the presence of cube roots, \\(^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}\\) expands to \\(\\sqrt[3]{6}\\).\n\nNow we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{2^{\\frac{8}{3}} + 8 \\cdot 3^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\cdot 2^{\\frac{1}{2}} - 6^{\\frac{2}{3}}}{3^{\\frac{4}{3}} - 6^{\\frac{2}{3}}}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final simplified form (in lowest terms) of the given fraction is:\n\\[\n\\frac{8 + 2 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 3^{\\frac{1}{3}} + 16^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{18^{\\frac{2}{3}} - 6^{\\frac{2}{3}}}\n\\]\nIn the form \\(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{A} + \\sqrt[3]{B}}{\\sqrt[3]{C}}\\):\n\nFinally,\n\\[ \\boxed{2 + 6 + 18 = 26} \\]",
